    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Aeva’s 4D LiDAR platform is gaining diversified adoption beyond passenger vehicles, with growing traction in autonomous trucking (Daimler Truck), defense (Forterra), infrastructure (CityOS), and factory automation (Nikon). This broadening end-market base is driving record revenue and supporting a physical AI enablement narrative. However, the momentum is partially offset by shifting OEM production timelines, which inject uncertainty into volume ramp expectations.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered tangible milestones, including production-intent Atlas sensors to Daimler Truck and integration with a major European passenger OEM, while proactively expanding into defense and industrial niches. Yet, earnings call revelations of adjusted production schedules and missed manufacturing capacity goals expose a gap between strategic announcements and operational execution. These contradictions could weigh on management credibility until timeline stability and manufacturing scaling are more clearly demonstrated.",
